@startuml SandboxInstanceLifecycle
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
' purpose: how the working directory selects a sandbox and where launch, reuse, teardown, and cleanup need ownership
' covers: defs/README.md
' covers: internal/run/run.go
' covers: internal/workspace/mount.go
' covers: internal/sbx/run.go
' covers: internal/sbx/list.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/launch_receipt.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/teardown.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/claude_mcp.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/opencode_engine.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/browser.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/verbs.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/clean.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/verbs.go
' See kit-lifecycle.puml for receipts and retirement and clone-workspace.puml for Git carry.
' See _spec/_plans/session-continuity.puml for the proposed retention change.
'
' DESIGN INTENT
' One ordinary name per target and workspace gives a retry a place to find
' the previous VM, its create-time settings, and any work it still holds.
' Proveo writes a new run ID, kit, and transcript for each invocation.
' It can therefore remove a VM after recovering its work and reuse the same
' name later. Docker sbx keeps its sandbox after the agent exits and supports
' several same-workspace VMs through distinct names. Proveo's ordinary CLI
' derives the name and has no user-supplied sandbox-name flag.
' Sources: https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/usage/#reconnect-and-name-sandboxes
'          https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/workflows/git/#clone-mode
'          https://github.com/docker/sbx-releases/issues/775#issuecomment-6445241506
'
' WORKSPACE IDENTITY AND PARALLEL RUNS
' The invocation directory supplies the default. --input and --scope can
' change the effective workspace. The ordinary name combines the target
' with the first four bytes of SHA-256 of the primary workspace path.
' A linked-worktree clone keys on the linked worktree root and uses the main
' checkout as sbx's clone source. The seed recreates the worktree at its own
' path inside the guest and selects its ref. Sibling worktrees therefore
' produce distinct names. A dry run with real sibling worktrees confirmed
' both names, the shared clone source and each guest path and ref.
' Changing branches in the same folder keeps the name. A normal kept clone
' follows the host ref at creation and the receipt does not track its new
' host tip. A changed linked-worktree ref can mark the kit or env stale.
' Different targets in one directory have different names. The browser
' add-on gives an unnamed browser run a run-specific name and a named
' profile a name derived from target, workspace and profile. A named
' profile has a host lease, checks its recorded sandbox ID when present,
' and rejects reuse unless the sandbox is stopped, created or exited.
' Worktrees are the ordinary same-target path to parallel runs with distinct
' checkout paths. Separate clone VMs isolate their main checkouts. Direct
' mode binds host paths. Both modes can still share writable home or extra
' mounts, Git metadata or host ports. Hermes shares its durable home across
' workspaces. In-guest worktrees isolate files while sharing the VM's fate.
'
' STALE, KEPT, AND ORPHANED
' Stale means the current create settings differ from the receipt, or the
' receipt is missing. It does not mean idle or old. The comparison covers
' agent, image, kit, clone mode, mounts and env. It does not directly compare
' publish rules, CPU or memory. A matching receipt leads to name-only
' reattachment with the new agent command and the old VM settings.
' A headed stale run asks before replacement. An unattended run retires a
' stopped sandbox and generally reuses a running one with a warning. Claude
' Code refuses live reuse. A persistent browser profile refuses settings
' drift. Retirement carries recoverable work and state before removal.
' Git and state recovery may start a stopped VM when they invoke sbx exec.
' Ordinary success lifts clone work and output, saves state, and removes the
' VM. Failures or incomplete carry, save or removal can leave it behind.
' OpenCode keeps its engine for SQLite history. A named browser profile
' stops and keeps its VM for the profile data.
' [Inference] An unnamed OpenCode browser run can retain a fresh engine on
' every clean exit. Its next invocation chooses a different name, and the
' normal OpenCode retention path clears the kept-result entry.
' A failed create or a killed host process can leave an sbx VM without a
' kept-result entry. An ordinary successful removal can leave its receipt.
' The launch path compares receipts only when it believes a VM exists.
' `sbx ls` is the VM inventory. `proveo rm` lists recorded kept results.
' `proveo rm <name>` carries work and state first and requires `--stop` for
' a running VM. `proveo clean` reclaims host artifacts and reconciles the
' results index. Its `--tools` check consults sbx liveness; it never sweeps
' sbx VMs. Clean protects run directories by their process PID and pins
' those recorded by named profiles. An ordinary kept VM can still depend
' on its old run directory, for example for a staged clone env or home files.
'
' RUNTIME JUDGMENT
' The stable name keeps resume discoverable and carry-before-remove protects
' guest work. The name alone cannot establish who owns the VM. Ordinary
' launches can overlap between lookup, receipt write, create and teardown.
' A launch can write the intended receipt before creation succeeds. Ordinary
' receipts have no sandbox ID binding. A failed listing can look like an
' existing but stopped VM because Exists and Running default differently.
' [Inference] Two callers can overwrite the receipt or race to create the
' name. If both attach, one can retire or remove a VM while the other uses
' it. A stopped-only check has the same gap before the next attach. A keep
' decision preserves a VM even when clean may reclaim its backing paths.
' [Inference] A 32-bit name suffix can collide. Treat the resolved workspace
' path and sbx ID as ownership evidence before reusing or mutating a name.
' Recommended boundary: one owning Proveo invocation per ordinary sandbox
' name. Extend the named-profile host lease to cover lookup through teardown
' and explicit removal. Require reliable inventory before mutation and bind
' the receipt to the created sandbox ID. Protect run directories referenced
' by existing VMs. This fits the pwd default without a session registry.
' Direct sbx sessions bypass a Proveo lease. A running VM without a Proveo
' owner needs an explicit recovery path before another run takes it over.
' If kept VMs become the default, the lease still gates stop and retire.
' Keep project-scoped defaults in defs/README.md. Build paths, agent home,
' durable state and managed tools keep their own explicit scope.
'
' Verification: CLI --print with one repository and two linked worktrees;
' launch_receipt_test.go, worktree_clone_test.go, browser_test.go,
' teardown_end_test.go, verbs_test.go and clean_run_state_test.go.
' [Unverified] Live sbx scheduling and race reproduction on this checkout.

title sbx instance lifecycle and workspace ownership

actor Operator as OP
participant "proveo run" as RUN
participant "launch receipt" as RECEIPT
participant "sbx" as SBX

OP -> RUN : launch from the chosen directory
RUN -> RUN : resolve workspace and sandbox name
RUN -> SBX : look up name and status
RUN -> RECEIPT : compare create settings for a kept VM
break launch refused by policy or operator
  RUN --> OP : report the refusal
end
alt fresh name or approved retirement
  opt retiring a previous VM
    RUN -> SBX : carry work and state, then remove
  end
  RUN -> RECEIPT : record intended create settings
  RUN -> SBX : create with the rendered kit
else reuse allowed
  RUN -> RUN : keep the stored VM settings
end
RUN -> SBX : run by name with the agent command
SBX --> RUN : agent exits or launch is stopped
RUN -> SBX : carry clone work, output and state
alt ordinary clean end
  RUN -> SBX : remove VM by name
else named browser profile
  RUN -> SBX : stop the VM and retain profile data
else retained VM or recovery needed
  RUN --> OP : report why the VM stays
end
@enduml
